// agentgateway mcpAuthorization rule: calculate_* tools need an authenticated operator.
//
// has(jwt.roles) so a token with a subject but no `roles` claim is a clean "no match"
// (deny) rather than a CEL evaluation error. jwt.roles.exists(...) requires a list, so a
// string claim cannot substring-match "operator".
//
// `jwt.roles` must be a top-level array claim. Keycloak puts realm roles under
// realm_access.roles by default; map them to a top-level `roles` claim with a realm-role mapper
// (tests/test_keycloak.py does this) or change the expression to read the nested claim.
//
// EDIT: the tool prefix and the role name.

mcp.tool.name.startsWith("calculate_") && has(jwt.sub) && has(jwt.roles) && jwt.roles.exists(r, r == "operator")
